                      (    forth6809.asm):08364                                   ; (a real discard of the loop-control frame).
                      (    forth6809.asm):08365                                   ; EXIT's own EXITUNLOOP mechanism already
                      (    forth6809.asm):08366                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):08367                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):08368                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):08369                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):08370                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):08371                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):08372                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):08373                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):08374                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):08375                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):08376                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):08377                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):08378                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):08379                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):08380                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):08381                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):08382                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):08383                                   ; a second, conflicting discard mechanism.
